  "title": "Namaz-e-Mayyat",
  "data": "Shorter Form\nLay the body on its back. Stand facing the qiblah, with its head to your right.\nIt is recommended to stand level with the middle of a man's body, or the chest of a woman's, and to take off your shoes.\nWudu is not required, but it is recommended; if water, a way to use it, or time for it is lacking, tayammum is recommended.\nMake the intention, then say the takbir (Allahu Akbar) five times, raising the hands to the ears with each.\nAfter the first Takbir, say:\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللهُ وَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَّسُوْلُ اللهِ.\nASH-HADU AL LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WA ASH-HADU ANNA MUHAMMADAR RASOOLULLAAH\nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\nAfter the second Takbir, say the Salawat:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ.\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.\nAfter the third Takbir, pray for the faithful believers:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ.\nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LIL MU'MINEENA WAL MU'MINAAT\nO Allah, forgive the believing men and the believing women.\nAfter the fourth Takbir, pray for the deceased:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِهٰذَا الْمَيِّتِ.\nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LIHAADHAL MAYYIT\nO Allah, forgive this deceased person.\nThen recite the fifth Takbir and conclude the prayer.",
  "tabs": [
    "Fuller Form\nMake the intention, then say:\nاَللهُ اَكْبَرُ\nALLAAHU AKBAR\nAllah is the Greatest.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADU AL LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, alone, without partner,\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUH\nand I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger,\nاَرْسَلَهٗ بِالْحَقِّ بَشِيْرًا وَّنَذِيْرًا بَيْنَ يَدَىِ السَّاعَةِ.\nARSALAHOO BIL HAQQI BASHEERAN WA NADHEERAN BAYNA YADAYIS SAA'AH\nwhom He sent with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner before the Hour.\nThen, for the second takbir, say:\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nALLAAHU AKBAR\nAllah is the Greatest.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَّبَارِكْ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَّارْحَمْ مُحَمَّدًا وَّاٰلَ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WA BAARIK A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WARHAM MUHAMMADAN WA AALA MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, grant abundance to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, and have mercy on Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nكَاَفْضَلِ مَا صَلَّيْتَ وَبَارَكْتَ وَتَرَحَّمْتَ عَلٰى اِبْرٰهِيْمَ وَاٰلِ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ اِنَّكَ حَمِيْدٌ مَّجِيْدٌ\nKA-AFDALI MAA SALLAYTA WA BAARAKTA WA TARAHHAMTA A'LAA IBRAAHEEMA WA AALI IBRAAHEEMA INNAKA HAMEEDUM MAJEED\nin the best way You blessed, granted abundance to and had mercy on Ibrahim and the Household of Ibrahim; surely You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.\nوَصَلِّ عَلٰى جَمِيْعِ الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ وَالْمُرْسَلِيْنَ.\nWA SALLI A'LAA JAMEE'IL ANBIYAA'I WAL MURSALEEN\nAnd bless all the prophets and messengers.\nThen, for the third takbir, say:\nاَللهُ اَكْبَرُ\nALLAAHU AKBAR\nAllah is the Greatest.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ وَالْمُسْلِميْنَ وَالْمُسْلِمَاتِ\nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LIL MU'MINEENA WAL MU'MINAATI WAL MUSLIMEENA WAL MUSLIMAAT\nO Allah, forgive the believing men and the believing women, the Muslim men and the Muslim women,\nاَلْاَحْيَاۤءِ مِنْهُمْ وَالْاَمْوَاتِ\nAL-AHYAA'I MINHUM WAL AMWAAT\nthe living among them and the dead.\nتَابِعْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَهُمْ بِالْخَيْرَاتِ\nTAABI' BAYNANAA WA BAYNAHUM BIL KHAYRAAT\nJoin us and them with continuous good;\nاِنَّكَ مُجِيْبُ الدَّعَوَاتِ اِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْئٍ قَدِيْرٌ.\nINNAKA MUJEEBUD DA'AWAATI INNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nsurely You answer prayers; surely You have power over all things.\nThen, for the fourth takbir, pray for the deceased:\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nALLAAHU AKBAR\nAllah is the Greatest.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّ هٰذَا عَبْدُكَ وَابْنُ عَبْدِكَ وَابْنُ اَمَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNA HAADHAA A'BDUKA WABNU A'BDIKA WABNU AMATIK\nO Allah, this is Your servant, the son of Your servant and the son of Your maidservant.\nنَزَلَ بِكَ وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ مَنْزُوْلٍ بِهٖ\nNAZALA BIKA WA ANTA KHAYRU MANZOOLIN BIH\nHe has come to You, and You are the best One to come to.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّا لَا نَعْلَمُ مِنْهُ اِلَّا خَيْرًا وَاَنْتَ اَعْلَمُ بِهٖ مِنَّا\nALLAAHUMMA INNAA LAA NA'LAMU MINHU ILLAA KHAYRAN WA ANTA A'LAMU BIHEE MINNAA\nO Allah, we know nothing of him but good, and You know him better than we do.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنْ كَانَ مُحْسِنًا فَزِدْ فِىْ اِحْسَانِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA IN KAANA MUHSINAN FAZID FEE IHSAANIH\nO Allah, if he did good, increase his good,\nوَاِنْ كَانَ مُسِيْئًا فَتَجَاوَزْ عَنْهُ وَاغْفِرْ لَهٗ\nWA IN KAANA MUSEE'AN FATAJAAWAZ A'NHU WAGHFIR LAH\nand if he did wrong, overlook it and forgive him.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْهُ عِنْدَكَ فِىْ اَعْلٰی عِلِّيِّيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'LHU I'NDAKA FEE A'LAA I'LLIYYEEN\nO Allah, place him with You in the highest 'Illiyyin,\nوَاخْلُفْ عَلٰى اَهْلِهٖ فِى الْغَابِرِيْنَ\nWAKHLUF A'LAA AHLIHEE FIL GHAABIREEN\ntake his place for his family among those who remain,\nوَارْحَمْهُ بِرَحْمَتِكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ.\nWARHAMHU BIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nand have mercy on him by Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nThen say the fifth takbir and end the prayer.\nIf the deceased is a woman, say this instead after the fourth takbir:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّ هٰذِہِ اَمَتُكَ وَابْنَۃُ عَبْدِكَ وَابْنَۃُ اَمَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNA HAADHIHI AMATUKA WABNATU A'BDIKA WABNATU AMATIK\nO Allah, this is Your maidservant, the daughter of Your servant and the daughter of Your maidservant.\nنَزَلَتْ بِكَ وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ مَنْزُوْلٍ بِهٖ\nNAZALAT BIKA WA ANTA KHAYRU MANZOOLIN BIH\nShe has come to You, and You are the best One to come to.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّا لَا نَعْلَمُ مِنْهَا اِلَّا خَيْرًا وَاَنْتَ اَعْلَمُ بِهَا مِنَّا\nALLAAHUMMA INNAA LAA NA'LAMU MINHAA ILLAA KHAYRAN WA ANTA A'LAMU BIHAA MINNAA\nO Allah, we know nothing of her but good, and You know her better than we do.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنْ كَانَتْ مُحْسِنَۃً فَزِدْ فِىْ اِحْسَانِهَا\nALLAAHUMMA IN KAANAT MUHSINATAN FAZID FEE IHSAANIHAA\nO Allah, if she did good, increase her good,\nوَاِنْ كَانَتْ مُسِيْئَۃً فَتَجَاوَزْ عَنْهَا وَاغْفِرْ لَهَا\nWA IN KAANAT MUSEE'ATAN FATAJAAWAZ A'NHAA WAGHFIR LAHAA\nand if she did wrong, overlook it and forgive her.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْهَا عِنْدَكَ فِىْ اَعْلٰی عِلِّيِّيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'LHAA I'NDAKA FEE A'LAA I'LLIYYEEN\nO Allah, place her with You in the highest 'Illiyyin,\nوَاخْلُفْ عَلٰى اَهْلِهَا فِى الْغَابِرِيْنَ\nWAKHLUF A'LAA AHLIHAA FIL GHAABIREEN\ntake her place for her family among those who remain,\nوَارْحَمْهَا بِرَحْمَتِكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ.\nWARHAMHAA BIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nand have mercy on her by Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nIf the deceased is one of those deemed enfeebled in faith (mustad'af), say this instead after the fourth takbir:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلَّذِيْنَ تَابُوْا وَاتَّبَعُوْا سَبِيْلَكَ وَقِهِمْ عَذَابَ الْجَحِيْمِ.\nALLAAHUMMAGH FIR LILLADHEENA TAABOO WATTABA'OO SABEELAKA WA QIHIM A'DHAABAL JAHEEM\nO Allah, forgive those who repent and follow Your way, and protect them from the punishment of Hell.\nIf the deceased is a child who had not come of age, say this instead after the fourth takbir:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اجْعَلْهُ لِاَبَوَيْهِ وَلَنَا سَلَفًا وَفَرَطًا وَاَجْرًا.\nALLAAHUMMAJ A'LHU LI-ABAWAYHI WA LANAA SALAFAN WA FARATAN WA AJRAA\nO Allah, make him, for his parents and for us, a precursor, a forerunner and a reward."
